{# The icon affordances sitting on one sidebar row (queue item 35).

   Each one is a REAL menu item that named this row in its `attachTo` — it renders ONLY here, not
   also as a row of its own further down the same list (AdminMenuTreeBuilder::assemble() already
   dropped that row once this icon resolved) — so it still has its own route, its own label and its
   own permission, and the accessible name below is a true statement about where the link goes
   rather than a caption invented for a decoration. "New Bill", never "+": a screen reader reading
   out a column of plus signs tells nobody anything.

   A plain <a> with a real href, rendered server-side. Nothing here is script-injected and nothing
   needs JavaScript to work, which is the house rule (public/assets/js/app.js, tests/Functional/
   AdminNoJs*Cest.php) and is also the only way the reveal can be pure CSS.

   Reveal/hide is entirely in public/assets/css/app.css: opacity + visibility on
   `:hover, :focus-within`, never `display: none` — that would take the link out of the tab order
   and the accessibility tree altogether — and always visible below the sidebar's own touch
   breakpoint, where there is no hover to reveal anything with.

   The glyph is conditional and the link is not, which is the whole degrade rule in one line: an
   item naming no icon, or an icon this app does not have, still gets its button — same href, same
   accessible name, same hover and focus — just nothing drawn inside it. app.css gives the button a
   fixed 22x22 box precisely so that an empty one is still a real hit target and a real focus stop,
   rather than collapsing to zero width and being present in name only.

   `only` is deliberate: this partial needs nothing from the sidebar's context, and inheriting it
   would let a caller's `node`/`child` leak in and be rendered by mistake. #}
{% for affordance in affordances %}
    {% if affordance.requiresRole is null or is_granted(affordance.requiresRole) %}
        <a class="nav-affordance" href="{{ affordance.route is not null ? path(affordance.route, affordance.routeParams) : affordance.url }}" aria-label="{{ affordance.affordanceName }}" title="{{ affordance.affordanceName }}">{% if affordance.affordanceIconSvg is not null %}{{ affordance.affordanceIconSvg|raw }}{% endif %}</a>
    {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
